  m_Scene: {fileID: 102900000, guid: a4c8d90f9128111409d69eba82dc027f, type: 3}
  m_ScenePath: Assets/Examples/TheoJansen/TheoJansen.unity
  m_ExampleName: Theo Jansen
  m_Category: Joints
  m_Purpose: "Demonstrates a complex linkage of joints driven by a single motor. Theo Jansen's walking machine turns one wheel, and six legs built from hinge and distance joints turn that rotation into a walking step.\nThe wheel, chassis and legs share a negative contact group so they never touch each other, only the ground and the field of balls."
  m_Controls: "Left and Right arrow keys, or the Left and Right buttons: turn the motor one way or the other.\nSpace, or the Brake button: stop the motor.\nSpeed and Torque: how fast the motor turns and how much torque it has.\nDrag the machine to move it."
  m_Description: Theo Jansen's walking machine, where a motor turns a wheel that steps six linkage legs across a field of balls.
